    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262-a1">

                <pb facs="0390" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg310"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ehrman to Mr. Hill</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1902-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                25, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 329.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    your information, a copy of a letter received from Mr. W. A. Barney, consular
                    agent at Cali, Colombia, together with a letter from the firm of Holman &amp;
                    Shearer to Mr. Barney.</p>
                <p>I have no information in regard to this subject other than that which is set
                    forth in the inclosed letters.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your instructions, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Felix Ehrman</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States
                    Vice-Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
